.TH FLEET-CONFIG 1 "2026-11-21" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
fleet-config \- fleet.env checked against the settings the code reads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fleet\-config check
.RB [ \-\-env
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B fleet\-config list
.RB [ \-\-secrets ]
.RB [ \-\-by\-reader ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent fleet\-config check
.SH DESCRIPTION
Step 1 of splitting
.I fleet.env
(BACKLOG). The file holds about 165 settings, and every unit loads all of
it, so every lane carries every secret.
.B fleet\-config
shows what the file holds before anything is moved.
.PP
.B It never prints a value.
Only key names, counts and line numbers, so its output is safe to paste
into a ticket.
.PP
What the code reads comes from
.IR settings.manifest ,
installed beside the commands. For each setting it lists the programs that
read it, and whether it is a secret, when it is required, and its default.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Read
.I fleet.env
and report, in this order:
settings that are required and not set (or set to nothing);
settings no code reads, with the nearest known name, as for a typo;
keys set more than once (the last one wins);
lines that are not
.BR KEY=value ;
settings equal to their default, and settings set to nothing, which can be
removed; and each secret that is set, with the programs that read it.
.TP
.B list
Every setting the code reads, with its flags and readers.
.B \-\-secrets
lists only the secrets.
.B \-\-by\-reader
lists, for each program, how many settings and which secrets it reads: the
map step 2 of the split grants credentials from.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-env " FILE"
The file to check. Default:
.BR $FLEET_ENV ,
else
.IR /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No problems: nothing missing, unknown, duplicated or unreadable. Settings
that could be removed are not problems.
.TP
.B 1
At least one problem, the file could not be read, or the manifest was not
found.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent fleet\-config check
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent fleet\-config list \-\-by\-reader
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-agent (1),
RUNBOOK.md section 11m,
.IR scripts/settings\-manifest .
